description:
**Key Areas of Responsibilities**

* Reporting to Senior IT Procurement Manager
* Lead or support the RFx process end\\-to\\-end for IT/Business stakeholder departments for
* assigned IT sourcing projects;
* Perform contract negotiations with vendors until mutual agreement is reached. Ensure all
* business, technical, commercial and legal requirements are captured in the final contract;
* Perform financial analysis of assigned sourcing projects and prepare/present business
* cases to senior management;
* Collaborate with IT project managers and internal stakeholders to go through internal
* approval process, ensure all required documentations are properly in place and steps are
* followed;
* Regular reporting of all types procurement analytics and vendor spends analysis to senior
* management;
* Develop and maintain vendor (including potential vendor) relationships to ensure the
* company has a broad access to supply chain market in order to support the growth of the
* company;
* Manage vendor onboarding due diligence process and vendor ongoing reassessments;
* Continuous user training and communication of procurement policy and processes to
* Group IT users worldwide to ensure policy compliance and facilitate approval process

**Requirements**

* University degree in Procurement or IT or Computer Science, preferably qualifier in CIPS
* 5\\-10 years of working experience in technology procurement and vendor management in
* FSI, insurance or related sectors;
* Proven hands on experience in running RFx projects and associated stakeholder
* management;
* Working knowledge in various IT category management skills (hardware, software,
* telecom, professional services), contract negotiation and vendor management skills;
* Proficiency in procurement policy \\& best practices, and procurement software tool;
* Ability to identify user requirements and speak stakeholder languages;
* Good understanding of financial regulatory requirements, basic contract law, and basic
* accounting principles.
* Proficient in Microsoft Office \\& Excel
* Ability to work independently as well as in team environment.
* Excellent analytical, project management, and communication skills
* Fluency in both English and Mandarin

The West Kowloon Cultural District Authority welcomes exceptional talent with a passion to realise the vision and mission of making the West Kowloon Cultural District a prime local and international destination for arts, culture and entertainment.




**You Will Be Responsible For**
* administrating and supporting end user computing environment including Windows and Mac platform; as well as Cloud platform like Microsoft 365 and Azure;
* participating in solution and software evaluation, performance monitoring and diagnoses, identify and prevent potential issue proactively;
* preparing technical documents and reports, implementation proposals and user manual;
* working with and managing the vendor of IT projects and assisting in monitoring the implementation of IT projects;
* providing system ongoing technical support and assisting the management of IT helpdesk service;
* assisting in the management of IT service management processes, such as incident management, problem management, change management, and service request management;
* ensuring all IT support services are delivered in accordance with established service level agreements (SLAs);
* assisting the development of technology roadmap for Microsoft 365 (M365\\) and lead the team to manage and support all infrastructure and services such as MS Teams, Exchange Online and Intune;
* managing technology partners and vendors to deliver the required services;
* assist in the procurement of computing hardware, software, and peripherals, ensuring alignment within the Authority’s standards and cost optimization; and
* performing any other duties as assigned by the Authority.


**You Should**
* possess a recognised university degree or diploma in computer science, information technology or equivalent;
* at least 5 years of experience in the IT industry with focus on IT operation support;
* have strong experience in administering and supporting Windows, Mac, M365, Directory Services will be an advantage;
* have knowledge of IT service management frameworks, such as ITIL is preferred;
* familiar with the latest workplace technologies such as cloud computing, virtualization, and mobile device management;
* have ability to manage multiple projects and priorities in a fast\\-paced environment;
* certification of Microsoft 365 Administrator is preferred;
* have excellent communication and interpersonal skills; and
* be proficient in written and spoken English and Chinese.


 For interested parties, please submit your application with detailed CV on or before following date. Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. The review of applications will continue until post is filled.




 20\\-11\\-2025




 Data collected will only be used for job application processing. Your data may be accessed by our appointed recruitment consultants who have agreed to keep confidence of all personal data in not less than the standards applicable to us. Applicants not being invited for interview within 4 weeks from the submission date may assume their applications unsuccessful.




 All related information will be kept up to 24 months and all personal data will be destroyed afterwards.




 For more information, please visit https://www.westk.hk or contact:




 Jason Wong /\\+852 22000285

We are looking for high\\-calibre individuals to join the Information Technology Department for serving HKMC Insurance Limited (HKMCI), a wholly\\-owned subsidiary of The Hong Kong Mortgage Corporation Limited.










**Job Descriptions:** 



* Support and manage the operational support for critical cloud infrastructure, ensuring high availability, performance and stability;
* Support adoption and implementation of Cloud Infrastructure;
* Maintain and administer Windows Server environments, both on\\-premises and within Azure/AWS. Oversee and manage identity and access solutions, specifically Azure Active Directory (AAD);
* Implement best practices for Identity and Access Management (IAM), data protection, network security (e.g. firewalls, WAFs) and regulatory compliance across all cloud platforms;
* Support complex cloud\\-related projects, including large\\-scale cloud migrations and system integrations;
* Implement and utilise monitoring and alerting tools to track the health, performance and cost of the cloud infrastructure;
* Act as a subject matter expert and provide technical guidance to team members and other IT professionals;
* Engage in problem\\-solving process and incident management. Responsibilities include managing incident response, leading root cause analysis for major issues and continuously improving service uptime; and
* The employment will be on a 2\\-year contract term, subject to renewal.









**Requirements:** 



* Degree holder with major in Computer Science or related discipline;
* A minimum of 8 years of progressive experience in IT infrastructure;
* Hands\\-on experience with Microsoft Windows Server administration and managing hybrid or cloud\\-native identity and access solutions using Azure Active Directory (AAD);
* Solid experience in designing, implementing and maintaining robust, scalable and secure cloud infrastructure on both Azure and AWS. This includes proficiency with core services such as compute, storage, networking and security configurations;
* A strong command of automation and modern DevOps practices. Good scripting skills in languages such as Python or PowerShell;
* Proven ability to implement and enforce best practices for cloud governance and security. Experience should cover identity and access management (IAM), data protection, network security (firewalls, WAFs) and regulatory compliance;
* Relevant professional certifications, such as AWS Certified Solutions Architect, Azure Solutions Architect Expert, or ITIL, are highly preferred; and
* Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese









 Interested parties please send your full resume stating current and expected salary by
 **16 November 2025** 
 .










 Please visit http://www.hkmc.com.hk/eng/careers/job\\_openings.html for other application methods.










 Please ensure that all information provided to the HKMC Group is accurate, complete and updated. Data provided which is inaccurate or incomplete may influence the process and outcome of the recruitment exercise. Please read the HKMC Group Personal Information Collection Statement for Job Applicants at the HKMC website before completing the application form. Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Candidates not invited for interview within 8 weeks may consider their application unsuccessful.

The West Kowloon Cultural District Authority welcomes exceptional talent with a passion to realise the vision and mission of making the West Kowloon Cultural District a prime local and international destination for arts, culture and entertainment.




 The Manager, IT Operation is accountable for the strategic oversight and continuous advancement of the organization’s IT functions. This role entails leading a team of IT professionals, maintaining operational excellence in daily service delivery, and ensuring the reliability of critical IT infrastructure, including systems supporting IT and event operations. The position is pivotal in providing seamless support for all mission\\-critical technology assets, upholding operational integrity across the authority.




**You Will Be Responsible For**
* managing and monitoring the IT operations team to support the reliable and efficient delivery of IT services;
* developing and implementing operational policies, standards, and best practices to enhance IT service delivery;
* coordinating incident response, problem management, and root cause analysis for operational issues;
* collaborating with business units to align IT operations with business requirements and strategic objectives;
* developing and maintaining comprehensive Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) for all operational processes to facilitate knowledge transfer and continuity;
* developing the technology roadmap for Microsoft 365 (M365\\) and leading the team to manage and support all M365 services such as MS Teams, Exchange Online and Intune;
* managing the operation of critical IT infrastructure, including systems that support IT services, event operations and other essential services;
* overseeing client computing environments, including the deployment, configuration, and lifecycle management of desktops, laptops, and mobile devices;
* enabling and fostering collaboration with the IT infrastructure team and stakeholders to ensure seamless integration and operational excellence across all IT and AV operations;
* establishing and overseeing governance frameworks for IT and AV managed services, ensuring compliance with organizational standards, service quality, IT asset management and vendor performance;
* managing technology partners and vendors to deliver the required services;
* managing the budget and financials to deliver the optimal services to users; and
* performing any other duties from time to time as reasonably assigned by the Authority.


**You Should**
* possess a Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Computer Science, or related discipline;
* have at least 7 years of experience in IT operations, with 3\\+ years in a managerial or supervisory role;
* have strong experience in managing IT infrastructure, service delivery, and operational processes;
* be familiar with the latest workplace technologies such as cloud computing, virtualization, and mobile device management;
* be familiar with ITIL or similar IT service management frameworks is preferred;
* have excellent leadership, organizational, and problem\\-solving skills;
* have strong communication and stakeholder management abilities; and
* have good command of written and spoken English and Chinese.


 For interested parties, please submit your application with detailed CV on or before following date. Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. The review of applications will continue until post is filled.




